132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 106 0 R
/T (IPv6 privacy extensions allow IoT devices to rotate temporary addresses, reducing address-based tracking but complicating local security monitoring. Priv6Guard proposes a privacy-aware monitoring system that correlates security events through authenticated, short-lived local sessions and pseudonyms rather than permanent device identifiers. The system monitors IPv6 traffic, detects suspicious Router Advertisements and abnormal Neighbor Discovery Protocol \(NDP\) activity, and presents alerts through a web dashboard. A controlled five-device IPv6 LAN will be used to evaluate detection performance, session continuity, pseudonym expiration, and cross-tenant isolation.)
/E (IPv6 privacy extensions allow IoT devices to rotate temporary addresses, reducing address-based tracking but complicating local security monitoring. Priv6Guard proposes a privacy-aware monitoring system that correlates security events through authenticated, short-lived local sessions and pseudonyms rather than permanent device identifiers. The system monitors IPv6 traffic, detects suspicious Router Advertisements and abnormal Neighbor Discovery Protocol \(NDP\) activity, and presents alerts through a web dashboard. A controlled five-device IPv6 LAN will be used to evaluate detection performance, session continuity, pseudonym expiration, and cross-tenant isolation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
